  "grammar_explanations": [
    {
      "slug": "present simple: be (am/is/are) with adjectives",
      "title_form": "El verbo ser/estar con adjetivos",
      "title_target": "The verb to be with adjectives",
      "description_md_form": "En inglés, para decir cómo te sientes, usamos el verbo **to be** (ser/estar) con un **adjetivo**. Es muy simple: el verbo cambia según la persona.\n\n- **I am** happy. (Yo estoy feliz.)\n- **You are** tired. (Tú estás cansado.)\n- **He/She/It is** sad. (Él/Ella está triste.)\n\nEn conversación, usamos las formas cortas: **I'm**, **you're**, **he's**, etc. Por ejemplo: **I'm fine, thanks.**\n\nLa estructura es siempre: **sujeto + verbo to be + adjetivo**.",
      "description_md_target": "In English, to say how you feel, we use the verb **to be** with an **adjective**. It is very simple: the verb changes depending on the person.\n\n- **I am** happy.\n- **You are** tired.\n- **He/She/It is** sad.\n\nIn conversation, we use the short forms: **I'm**, **you're**, **he's**, etc. For example: **I'm fine, thanks.**\n\nThe structure is always: **subject + verb to be + adjective**.",
      "grammar_structure": "Subject + to be (am/is/are) + adjective",
      "conjugation_table": {
        "name": "present_simple_be",
        "headers": [
          "Pronombre",
          "Forma",
          "Forma corta"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "I",
            "am",
            "I'm"
          ],
          [
            "you",
            "are",
            "you're"
          ],
          [
            "he / she / it",
            "is",
            "he's / she's / it's"
          ],
          [
            "we",
            "are",
            "we're"
          ],
          [
            "they",
            "are",
            "they're"
          ]
        ]
      },
